  "caption": "Quinn went in for a high five, but one finger stayed politely curled. Gloves became a puzzle, and Grandpa Quokka had the same finger.\n\nKay's take: in Dupuytren's, tissue in the palm can thicken into a cord that slowly pulls a finger in. It's usually painless, often runs in families, and isn't caused by manual work.\n\nWhat can help: doing the tabletop test now and then (if your hand won't lie flat, talk with your GP), keeping the hand busy with normal gripping and carrying, and adapting tricky tasks. Stretching and massage won't reverse the cord, but hand therapy can help if treatment is ever needed.\n\nGet it checked if your hand won't lie flat, or washing, gloves or handshakes are getting harder.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
